\DOC LOCAL_JADD_SAFETY_TAC

\TYPE {LOCAL_JADD_SAFETY_TAC : string -> int -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Advances a symbolic-execution goal across a subroutine call by applying a named
assumption that is a universally quantified {ensures} specification, replacing
the current state's facts with those of the post-call state.

\DESCRIBE
{LOCAL_JADD_SAFETY_TAC assump_name n} takes a string {assump_name}, naming the
labelled assumption of the goal that holds the callee's {ensures} specification
to be applied, and an integer {n}, the index of the state produced by the step,
which is used to form the new state variable of the resulting goal. It applies
to a goal whose conclusion is an {eventually} claim about a state {xk} and
whose assumptions describe the registers, loaded program, memory footprint and
event trace of {xk}, along with labelled callee specifications. It yields
exactly one subgoal, whose conclusion is the same {eventually} claim about a
fresh state {x(n)}. The register-value, {bytes_loaded}, {read events},
stack-pointer and {MAYCHANGE} assumptions about the old state are dropped and
replaced by corresponding assumptions about the new state: an updated program
counter and stack pointer, a {read events} equation whose trace is extended by
a fresh trace variable {e1 ... en} for the call, two further assumptions
characterising that trace variable (its value in terms of the callee's event
function, and a memory-access-in-bounds fact about it), a widened {MAYCHANGE}
relation covering the callee's writes, and the surviving facts about the loaded
program and the unchanged memory cells. Pre-existing side conditions
(non-overlapping facts, earlier trace equations) and both labelled callee
specifications are kept, although their order in the assumption list changes.

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces this is the only outcome shown, and it always occurs on
goals of this {eventually} form carrying a named callee {ensures} assumption.

\ENDDOC
